# Component Structure (SHM)

This project uses **Shadcn UI** in `components/ui/` (single-file primitives) and feature folders under `components/`.

## components/ui/

- One file per primitive: **kebab-case.tsx** (e.g. `button.tsx`, `card.tsx`, `dialog.tsx`).
- Import with `@/components/ui/button`, etc.
- No mandatory one-folder-per-component here; flat files are fine.

## components/layout/

- Layout pieces: `sidebar.tsx`, `header.tsx`, etc. Single file or folder with related files.

## components/features/

- **One folder per feature/screen** (e.g. `timeline/`, `golden-temple/`, `ten-gurus/`).
- Feature-specific or larger components live here as kebab-case files: `timeline-table.tsx`, `timeline-form.tsx`, `edit-content-dialog.tsx`.
- Re-export public components from **`index.ts`** (barrel). Co-locate types next to the component when it helps.

**Guidelines:**

- One component per file (or small private sub-components in same file if needed).
- Use **@/** for imports (e.g. `@/components/ui/button`, `@/utils/auth-service`).
- New reusable pieces that don’t belong in `ui/` can get their own folder under `components/` with an `index.tsx` or barrel if needed.

## When to create a component folder

- Create a folder instead of a single file when:
  - The component has **visible subcomponents** (e.g. `Header`, `Footer`, `Item`).
  - You need **types, tests, stories, or styles** that are specific to this component.
  - The JSX or logic is getting large and you want to split it into clearer pieces.

Example:

```bash
components/user-card/
├── index.tsx              # Re-export main component + types
├── UserCard.tsx           # Main component
├── UserCardHeader.tsx     # Sub-component
├── UserCardFooter.tsx     # Sub-component
├── UserCard.types.ts      # Types/interfaces
└── UserCard.test.tsx      # Tests
```

## Subcomponent naming

- Name subcomponents with the **parent prefix** to keep search and imports clear:
  - `UserCardHeader.tsx`, `UserCardFooter.tsx`, `UserCardItem.tsx`
- Re-export public pieces from `index.tsx`:

```ts
// components/user-card/index.tsx
export { default as UserCard } from './UserCard';
export { default as UserCardHeader } from './UserCardHeader';
export { default as UserCardFooter } from './UserCardFooter';
export type { UserCardProps } from './UserCard.types';
```

- Keep **private-only** subcomponents in the same file as the parent when:
  - They are tiny helpers.
  - They are not reused outside that file.
